## Lessons Learned

This lab provided hands-on experience managing virtual infrastructure from a Linux host rather than relying exclusively on a graphical virtualization interface.

Using `virsh` also provided practical experience inspecting VM resources and configuration from the command line.

The lab establishes the foundation for additional security work involving network segmentation, monitoring, traffic analysis, vulnerability management, and Windows/Linux security testing.

## Verification Commands

The VM configuration was verified using libvirt command-line tools:

```bash
virsh dominfo lab-ubuntu01
virsh dominfo lab-windows01

virsh domblklist lab-ubuntu01
virsh domblklist lab-windows01

virsh domblkinfo lab-ubuntu01 vda
virsh domblkinfo lab-windows01 sda

virsh domiflist lab-ubuntu01
virsh domiflist lab-windows01
```

These commands were used to verify CPU, memory, storage, virtual disk capacity, and virtual network adapter configuration.
